                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>By tendering articles and/or documents for shipment(''shipment'') under this Consignment Note (''CN'')via Yusen Logistics India Pvt. Ltd. (''YUSEN'') which term shall include its authorised agents and afﬁliated companies, their ofﬁcers, directors and employees, the shipper("Shipper")ontis be half and on half of anyone else with anterestin the Shipment, agrees to the Terms and Conditions stated here in .Noagent, employee or servant of YUSEN or of the Shipper shall after or modify these Terms &amp; conditions.

The liability of YUSEN and its employees and agents is strictly limited to the amount stated in these Terms and Conditions. The Shipper is therefore advised to ensure that its interest are fully protected in all events by purchasing all risk insurance cover from any insurer.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>1	THE CONSIGNMENT NOTES</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
1.1	The CN is non-negotiable and the shipper acknowledges that it has been prepared by the shipper or YUSEN on behalf of shipper.
1.2	The shipper warrants that it is the owner of the shipment or that it is the authorized agent of he owner of the shipment
1.3	The shipper hereby accepts these terms and conditions of itself and as agent fo and on behalf of any other person having any interest in the shipment.
1.4	The shipment is carried entirely at the risk of the shipper.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>2.	SHIPPER'S OBLIGATIONS AND ACKNOWLEDGMENTS</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
2.1	The shipper warrents that each article in the shipment is properly described on this CN, that it does not contain any of the article declared by YUSEN to be unacceptable for carriage as speciﬁed CN, that it does not contain any of the articles declared by YUSEN to be unacceptable for carriage as speciﬁed under clause 11 below and that the shipment is properly packed, marked and addessed to ensure safe carriage, with normal care in handling.
2.2	The shipper is responsible for the correctness of the particulars and statements relating to the shipment mentioned in the CN, The shipper indemniﬁes YUSEN against all damage suffered by YUSEN or any other person to whom YUSEN is liable, by reason of the irregularity, incorrectness or incompleteness of the particulars and statements furnished by the shipper.
2.3	Im the event :
2.3.1	an article in the shipment its declared by YUSEN to be unacceptable,
2.3.2	the shipper has undervalued or mis declared the value of the shipment (whether intentionally or otherwise):
2.3.3	the consignee refuses delivery or to pay on delivery;
2.3.4	the   consignee   cannot   be    reasonably    indentiﬁed    or    location; YUSEN shall use reasonable efforts to return the shipment to shipper at shipper's cost, falling which, the shipper hereby authorized YUSEN to return the shipment to shipper at shipper's cost, falling which, the any liability whatsoever to the shipper or anyone else. Upon accounting to the shipper for any balance remaining after payment ofany sums due to yusen and any costs of retention disposal or sale, yusen shall be discharged of any liability whatsoever in respect of the shipment. The shipper shall Indemnify YUSEN against all claims, demands, proceedings, ﬁnes, penalties, damages, costs and expenses suffered by YUSEN or by any other person to who YUSEN is liable in respect hereof;
2.4	The shipper shall be solely responsible for all documents in connection with shipment and all ﬁnes, penalties, costs, expenses, demurrage charges, detention charges etc. imposed on the shipment shall be payable by the shipper alone.
2.5	Unless stated otherwise in writing, the shipment is carried by YUSEN, from the booking ofﬁce of YUSEN or from shipper's door from the address given in the consignment note up to the address shown on this CN.
2.6	In the event the Shipment has to be rerouted / redirected / returned for any reason whatsoever, the Shipper shall pay in advance all charges levied by YUSEN for such rerouting / redirected / return, and also any ﬁnes, Penalties. damages, costs, expenses, including, but not limited to, Octroi, Central, State and local taxes etc and also provide necessary document for such change.
2.7	The shipper acknowledges that YUSEN is not a common carrier. YUSEN reserves that right to refuse the carriage of any shipment for any person or the carriage of any class of articles, at its sole discretion, without assigning any reason whatsoever.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>3	RIGHT OF INSPECTION OF SHIPMENT</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
3.1	YUSEN shall have the right, but not the obligation, to inspect and/or to open the shipment at its sole discretion without giving notice whatsoever to the shipper.
3.2	YUSEN shall have the right to re-weight, re-measure and re-classify the shipment and to re-calculate the freight and other charges payable before delivery of the shipment in accordance with the provisions hereof. (except where YUSEN has agreed to provide credit terms to the shipper).

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>4	LIEN ON GOODS SHIPPED</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
4.1	YUSEN shall have a general lien on all articles in the possession custody or control for any mories whatsoever due from the shipper and such general lien shall extend to all freight charges, duties, ﬁnes, penalties, damages, costs, expenses, including but not limited to, Octroi, central, state and local taxes or any other charges of any kind arising out of carriage hereunder.
4.2	YUSEN shall be entitled to detain any shipment at the shippers own risk until such dues are paid and, without prejudice to YUSEN's other legal remedies to recover its dues, YUSEN shall be entitled, after giving 7 (Seven) day's notice to the shipper to sell the articles by public auction, tender, private agreement or otherwise or even destroy the goods as agent for and at the expenses of the shipper and apply the proceeds in or towards the payment of such sums. Upon accounting to the shipper for any balance remaining after payment of any sums due to YUSEN shall be discharged of any liability whatsoever in respect of the shipment.
4.3	YUSEN does not carry any perishable articles, However, in case of perishable article, YUSEN shall have the right to dispose off/sell the same immediately and without any notice and the shipper shall keep YUSEN indemniﬁed against all claims charges and expenses incurred by YUSEN due to such perishable articles carried by YUSEN.</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                          </TextRuns>
                          <Style />
                        </Paragraph>
                      </Paragraphs>
                      <rd:DefaultName>Textbox26</rd:DefaultName>
                      <Style>
                        <Border>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                        </Border>
                        <TopBorder>
                          <Color>Black</Color>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                          <Width>1pt</Width>
                        </TopBorder>
                        <BottomBorder>
                          <Color>Black</Color>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                          <Width>1pt</Width>
                        </BottomBorder>
                        <LeftBorder>
                          <Color>Black</Color>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                          <Width>1pt</Width>
                        </LeftBorder>
                        <RightBorder>
                          <Color>Black</Color>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                          <Width>1pt</Width>
                        </RightBorder>
                        <PaddingLeft>2pt</PaddingLeft>
                        <PaddingRight>2pt</PaddingRight>
                        <PaddingTop>2pt</PaddingTop>
                        <PaddingBottom>2pt</PaddingBottom>
                      </Style>
                    </Textbox>
                  </CellContents>
                </TablixCell>
                <TablixCell>
                  <CellContents>
                    <Textbox Name="Textbox30">
                      <CanGrow>true</CanGrow>
                      <KeepTogether>true</KeepTogether>
                      <Paragraphs>
                        <Paragraph>
                          <TextRuns>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>5.	LIMITATION IF LIABILITY</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
5.1	The liability if YUSEN for any loss or damage to the shipments limited to the lowest of;
a)	The amount of loss or damage to the shipment actually sustained; or
b)	The deemed value of the shipment as determined under clauses 6 hereof without regard to its commercial utility or special value to the shipper.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>6	DEEMED VALUE</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
6.1	The deemed value of the shipment carried hereunder shall be ascertained by reference to its cost for repair or replacement, resale or fair market value at the time and place of shipment and in any event shall not exceed the original cost of the article actually paid by the shipper plus 10% of such cost but alway subject to an overall limit of Rs. 1000/- (Rupees one thousand only).

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>7	CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES EXCLUDED</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
7.1	Notwithstanding anything contained herein, YUSEN shall not be liable in any event for any consequential or special damages or other indirect loss, howsoever arising whether or not YUSEN has acknowledged such damages might occure, including, but not limited to loss of income, proﬁts, interest, utility or loss market.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>8	LIABILITY NOT ASSUMED</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
8.1	YUSEN will endeavor to exercise the best efforts to provide expeditious delivery in accordance with the regular delivery schedules.
8.2	YUSEN shall not be liable under any circumstances, for delay in pickup, carriage or delivery of the shipment, regardless of cause of such delay. No claims whatsoever in this regards shall be entertained by YUSEN at any point of time.
8.3	YUSEN shall also not be liable for any loss, damage, mis-delivery or non-delivery;
a)	Due to acts of god, force majeure or any cause reasonably beyond the control of YUSEN or;
b)	Caused by;
(I)	The act, default or omission of the shipper, the consignee or any party who claims an interest in the shipment (including violation of any of these terms and conditions) or of any other person, particularly a person to who the shipment is tendered by YUSEN for carriage to any location not regularly served by YUSEN, regardless to whether the shipper requested or had knowledge of such third party delivery arrangements,
(II)	The nature of the shipment or any defect it's characteristics or inherent vice thereof.
(III)	Electrical or magnetic injury, erasure or such damage to electronic or photographic images or recordings in any form
(IV)	Government ofﬁcials I discharge of their ofﬁcial duties such as customs/Taxation/Octroi inspection etc.
8.4	The shipper/consignee are jointly and severally responsive for handling over all the documents relating to the shipment (''transit document'') to YUSEN at the booking ofﬁces of YUSEN. YUSEN will take all reasonable care for safe handling of the transit documents.
8.5	In the event transit documents such as excise gate passes or sales tax permits etc, are misplaces by the employees/agents of YUSEN. YUSEN will notify the shipper/consignee of such missing documents. YUSEN shall not be responsible and/or liable for any loss or damage whatsoever caused to the shipper/ consignee in respect hereof.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>9	CLAIMS</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
9.1	Acceptance of the shipment by the consignee at the time of delivery without any remark will constitute a clean delivery and complete discharge of the contract of carriage by YUSEN and its liability arising therefrom.
9.2	Claims for loss / damage to the shipment, if any, must be brought by the consignee and delivered in writing to the nearest booking ofﬁce of YUSEN to the location at which the shipment is accepted within 14days of the date of such acceptance, falling which, YUSEN shall have no liability whatsoever. No claim shall be entertained by YUSEN outside of this time limit and no communication shall be entertained by YUSEN beyond said period.
9.3	As a condition for YUSEN considering any claim for loss/damage, the consignee must take the contents, original cartoons and packaging avaliable for inspection by YUSEN, which must be reatined until the claim is concluded. YUSEN reserve the right to inspect the alleged damaged shipment and to retrieve it for inspection at YUSEN booking ofﬁce, YUSEN shall be entitled to require proff in respect of any claim that the shipment was undamaged when carriage commenced.
9.4	Claims are limited to one claim per shipment settlement of which will be full and ﬁnal settlement for all loss or damage in connection therewith.
9.5	No claim for loss or damage will be entertained until all charges / payable hereunder have been paid, The shipper shall not deduct any claim amount form any charges owned to YUSEN.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>10.	MODE OF CARRIAGE</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
10.1	Wherever applicable, YUSEN reserves the right to arrange carriage of shipment by the mode of carriage best suitable for expeditious delivery.
10.2	YUSEN reserves to itself the right without assigning any reason whatsoever to charge from any usual or customary route and to carry the shipment by any other route, it may think ﬁt.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>11	MATERIAL NOT ACCEPTABLE FOR TRANSPORTATION</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
11.1	The following articles will not be accepted fo carriage.
a)	Hazardous and dangerous goods as per the list avaliable withe the booking ofﬁces of YUSEN.
b)	Chemicals drugs (provided however, such shipments may be accepted if they do not fail under the category of Hazardous and dangerous goods and the shipper provides a declaration in writing to the effect that the contents are harmless and non-inﬂammable.
c)	Precious cargo in the form of gold, bullion, silver, jewellery, gems, precious stones and other precious metals, currencynotes, travelers cheque, antiques, stamps.
d)	Perishable, live stocks, human remains, ﬁrearms, drugs, lewd, obscene or pornographic materials.
e)	Items the carriage of which are prohibited by nay law, stalute or regulation.
f)	Any item as many form time to time be notiﬁed by YUSEN to be restricted and / or banned and / or
</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Normal</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                          </TextRuns>
                          <Style />
                        </Paragraph>
                      </Paragraphs>
                      <rd:DefaultName>Textbox30</rd:DefaultName>
                      <Style>
                        <Border>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                        </Border>
                        <TopBorder>
                          <Color>Black</Color>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                          <Width>1pt</Width>
                        </TopBorder>
                        <BottomBorder>
                          <Color>Black</Color>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                          <Width>1pt</Width>
                        </BottomBorder>
                        <LeftBorder>
                          <Color>Black</Color>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                          <Width>1pt</Width>
                        </LeftBorder>
                        <RightBorder>
                          <Color>Black</Color>
                          <Style>Solid</Style>
                          <Width>1pt</Width>
                        </RightBorder>
                        <PaddingLeft>2pt</PaddingLeft>
                        <PaddingRight>2pt</PaddingRight>
                        <PaddingTop>2pt</PaddingTop>
                        <PaddingBottom>2pt</PaddingBottom>
                      </Style>
                    </Textbox>
                  </CellContents>
                </TablixCell>
                <TablixCell>
                  <CellContents>
                    <Textbox Name="Textbox34">
                      <CanGrow>true</CanGrow>
                      <KeepTogether>true</KeepTogether>
                      <Paragraphs>
                        <Paragraph>
                          <TextRuns>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>11.1	The shipper shall indemnify YUSEN against all claim, demands, proceedings, ﬁnes, penalties, damage, costs and expenses suffered by YUSEN or by any other person to whom YUSEN is liable in respect hereof whether or not the shipper was aware of the nature of such articles.
11.2	YUSEN reserve the right to refuse, hold cancel, postpone or return the shipment at any time if the shipment would in the sole and exclusive view of YUSEN be likely to cause damage or delay to other shipments.
11.3	The fact that YUSEN accepts a shipment does not means that such shipment conﬁrms to applicable law and regulations or to these terms and conditions.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>12	UNDELIVERED OR UNCLAIMED CONSIGNMENTS</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
12.1	A shipment shall be considered to be undelivered if;
a)	The consignee address is incomplete, illegible, incorrect or cannot be located.
b)	The consignee fails or refuses to accept delivery or sign or pay for delivery within a period of 10 (ten) days from the date of attempt to deliver the shipments made.
c)	If would likely cause damage of delay to other shipments.
d)	If contains prohibited items.
e)	It contents or packaging are damaged to the extent that re-wrapping is not possible.
f)	It is detained or otherwise unable to clear local ot state boundaries.
12.2	In case a shipment is undelivered ot unclaimed, YUSEN shall notify the shipper in writing requiring it to remove the shipment within a period of 15(ﬁfteen) days form the date of receipt of the notice. YUSEN shall have the right, but not the obligation, to sell such consignment without any further notice to the shipper or the consignee, as the case may be without incurring any liability whatsoever to the shipper / consignee or any other person. Upon accounting to the shipper for any balance remaining after payment of any sums due sums due to YUSEN and any cost of sale. YUSEN shall be discharged of any liability whatsoever in respect of the shipment. The shipper shall indemnify YUSEN against all claim respect of the shipment. The shipper shall indemnify YUSEN against all claim, demands, proceedings, ﬁnes. penalties, damage, costs and expenses suffered by YUSEN or by any other person to whom YUSEN is liable in respect thereof.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>13.SERVICE TAX</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
13.1	The shipper warrants that it shall declare;
a)	The service tax registration number of consignee.
b)	Its registration number under sales tax/VAT and that of the consignee.
c)	Its excise registration details and that of the consignee.
13.2	If the shipment is detained for non-provision of information as mandated in clause 13.1, the shipper / consignee will be solely and exclusively liable for all consequences of such detention and the shipper shall indemnify YUSEN against all claims, demands, proceeding, ﬁnes, penalties, damage, cost and expenses suffered by YUSEN or by any other person to whom YUSEN in respect hereof.
13.3	In the event of non-compliance with the provisions of clause 13.1 above YUSEN shall charge service tax to the shipper/ consignee paying freight charges. In any matters relating to sale tax or value service tax the responsibility rests solely with the consigner / consignee and the transport operator shall in no way be liable, accountable or penalized for the same.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>14	SCHEDULE OF  DEMURRAGE  CHARGES </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                          </TextRuns>
                          <Style />
                        </Paragraph>
                        <Paragraph>
                          <TextRuns>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>Demurrage chargeable after 7 (Seven) days of from the date of arrival @ Rs. 5 per KG on weight charged or per vehicle rate in case if it's a full truck load

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>15	JURISDICTION</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
Any claim or dispute arising between the parties as to the performance or non-performance of the foregoing terms and conditions shall be subject to the sole and exclusive jurisdiction of the courts at Mumbai, without regards to principles of conﬂict of laws.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>16	NON-WAIVER    </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value xml:space="preserve">                                                          </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                          </TextRuns>
                          <Style />
                        </Paragraph>
                        <Paragraph>
                          <TextRuns>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>Any failure by YUSEN to enforce or apply a provision of these terms does not constitute a waiver of that provision and does not otherwise impair YUSEN's right to enforce such provision.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>17.   PREVAILING   </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value xml:space="preserve">                                                       </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                          </TextRuns>
                          <Style />
                        </Paragraph>
                        <Paragraph>
                          <TextRuns>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>PARTY If the shipper/ YUSEN commences an action against the other to interpret or enforce any of the term of these terms and conditions or as a result of a breach by the other of any of its terms, the prevailing party shall be entitled to recover from the non-prevailing party reasonable attorney's fees, costs and expenses incurred by the prevailing party in connection with such action.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>18	SEVERABILITY  </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value xml:space="preserve">                                                        </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                          </TextRuns>
                          <Style />
                        </Paragraph>
                        <Paragraph>
                          <TextRuns>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value> If any provision of these terms and conditions is determined to be invalid or unenforceable in whole or in part, such invalidity or unenforceability shall attach only to such provision or part of such provision and the remaining part of such provision and all other provisions of these terms and conditions shall continue to remain in full force and effect.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>19	ALTERNATION     </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value xml:space="preserve">                                                </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                          </TextRuns>
                          <Style />
                        </Paragraph>
                        <Paragraph>
                          <TextRuns>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value> YUSEN reserve the right to unilaterally modify. amend, change or supplement these terms and conditions without notice. These terms and conditions are published in printed form and are avaliable at Yusen Logistics (India) Private Limited. No.201-11, II nd ﬂoor, Palm Court, Sukhrail Chowk, Gurgaon, India -122001.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>20	REMEDIES   </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value xml:space="preserve">                                               </Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                          </TextRuns>
                          <Style />
                        </Paragraph>
                        <Paragraph>
                          <TextRuns>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>CUMULATIVE The right and remedies given in these terms and conditions shall be deemed cumulative and the exercise of one of such right / remedies shall not operate to bar the exercise of any other right and remedies reserved under the provisions of these terms and conditions or given by law or inequity.

</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>21	ENTIRE AGREEMENT</Value>
                              <Style>
                                <FontSize>8pt</FontSize>
                                <FontWeight>Bold</FontWeight>
                              </Style>
                            </TextRun>
                            <TextRun>
                              <Value>
These terms and conditions set out the entire agreement and understaning between the shipper and YUSEN</Value>
                              <Style>
